# Playwright Hooks (TypeScript) - Notes

## What are Hooks?

Hooks are special methods that run before or after test execution.

They help reduce code duplication and manage setup/cleanup activities.

Common uses:

* Open application URL
* Login before tests
* Create test data
* Delete test data
* Logout after tests
* Capture screenshots/logs

---

## Types of Hooks

### 1. beforeEach()

Runs before every test.

### Syntax

```ts
test.beforeEach(async ({ page }) => {
    await page.goto('https://www.saucedemo.com/');
});
```

### Execution

```text
beforeEach
Test 1

beforeEach
Test 2

beforeEach
Test 3
```

### Use Cases

* Open application URL
* Login before every test
* Common setup required by all tests

### Example

```ts
test.beforeEach(async ({ page }) => {
    await page.goto('https://www.saucedemo.com/');
});

test('Valid Login', async ({ page }) => {
    // Test logic
});

test('Invalid Login', async ({ page }) => {
    // Test logic
});
```

---

## 2. afterEach()

Runs after every test.

### Syntax

```ts
test.afterEach(async () => {
    console.log('Test Finished');
});
```

### Execution

```text
beforeEach
Test 1
afterEach

beforeEach
Test 2
afterEach
```

### Use Cases

* Logout
* Cleanup actions
* Capture screenshots on failure
* Close resources

---

## 3. beforeAll()

Runs only once before all tests in a file.

### Syntax

```ts
test.beforeAll(async () => {
    console.log('Starting Test Execution');
});
```

### Execution

```text
beforeAll

Test 1
Test 2
Test 3
```

### Use Cases

* Create test data
* Environment setup
* API setup
* Database preparation

---

## 4. afterAll()

Runs only once after all tests are completed.

### Syntax

```ts
test.afterAll(async () => {
    console.log('Execution Finished');
});
```

### Execution

```text
beforeAll

Test 1
Test 2
Test 3

afterAll
```

### Use Cases

* Delete test data
* Generate reports
* Cleanup environment
* Close connections

---

## Complete Example

```ts
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test.beforeAll(async () => {
    console.log('Starting execution');
});

test.beforeEach(async ({ page }) => {
    await page.goto('https://www.saucedemo.com/');
});

test('Test 1', async ({ page }) => {
    // Test steps
});

test('Test 2', async ({ page }) => {
    // Test steps
});

test.afterEach(async () => {
    console.log('Test completed');
});

test.afterAll(async () => {
    console.log('Execution finished');
});
```

### Execution Order

```text
beforeAll

beforeEach
Test 1
afterEach

beforeEach
Test 2
afterEach

afterAll
```

---

## Difference Between beforeEach() and beforeAll()

| beforeEach()            | beforeAll()           |
| ----------------------- | --------------------- |
| Runs before every test  | Runs only once        |
| Executes multiple times | Executes one time     |
| Used for test setup     | Used for global setup |

### Example

If there are 3 tests:

```text
beforeEach -> 3 times
beforeAll -> 1 time
```

---

## Difference Between afterEach() and afterAll()

| afterEach()               | afterAll()                |
| ------------------------- | ------------------------- |
| Runs after every test     | Runs once after all tests |
| Used for cleanup per test | Used for global cleanup   |

### Example

If there are 3 tests:

```text
afterEach -> 3 times
afterAll -> 1 time
```

